  "prefLabel": "He-W 504.01 Definition",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 504.01 Definition.\n\n(a) “Medicaid for employed adults with disabilities (MEAD)” means a category of eligibility that allows certain individuals who are working to either retain or obtain medicaid eligibility.\n\nSource. #7644, eff 2-8-02; ss by #8292, eff 2-24-05; ss by #10321, eff 4-25-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w500.html"
}
